        "number": 1,
        "marks": 10,
        "text": "Mr. Tetteh keeps three hundred laying birds at Dodowa. Instead of buying ready-made feed he mixes his own ration from maize, wheat bran, fish meal, oyster shell, common salt and premix.\n\n**(a)** (i) What is a **ration**?  **[1 mark]**\n\n(ii) State **one** advantage of feeding animals on a balanced ration.  **[1 mark]**\n\n**(b)** Copy and complete the table below in your answer booklet.\n\n| Ingredient | Chief nutrient supplied |\n| --- | --- |\n| Maize | |\n| Fish meal | |\n| Oyster shell | |\n| Premix | |\n\n**(c)** Describe, in order, how Mr. Tetteh should mix one hundred kilogrammes of his ration by hand on the farm.\n\n---"
