        "number": 1,
        "marks": 10,
        "text": "During a health screening at a Basic 9 school in Sunyani, a nurse took a drop of blood from each pupil and examined it. She told the class that blood is a tissue made up of a liquid and several kinds of cell.\n\n**(a)** Name the **four** main components of human blood.\n\n**(b)** Copy and complete the table below in your answer booklet.\n\n| Component of blood | One function |\n| --- | --- |\n| Red blood cells | |\n| White blood cells | |\n| Platelets | |\n| Plasma | |\n\n**(c)** The nurse found that one pupil had very few red blood cells and looked pale.\n\n(i) Name the condition the pupil is suffering from.  **[1 mark]**\n\n(ii) Name **one** food that would help her.  **[1 mark]**\n\n**(d)** Explain why a person with very few red blood cells feels tired and becomes breathless after only a short walk.\n\n---"
