    "markingScheme": "*General rules: (1) Accept any other correct and relevant answer. (2) A factor must be clearly placed as natural or human where the question asks for one of them; a human activity given as a natural factor earns no mark. (3) In calculations, award the method mark for correct working even when the arithmetic that follows is wrong, and award the final mark only when the unit or the percentage sign is given. (4) Where a candidate gives more answers than are asked for, mark only the first ones up to the number required. (5) Do not deduct marks for spelling unless the meaning is changed.)*\n\n### Question 1 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [3 marks]\n\n- (i) **The average weather condition of a place over a long period** (1 mark).\n- (ii) **Weather changes from day to day; climate is the average over many years** (1 mark).\n- (iii) **A lasting change in the average weather pattern of a place or of the earth** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: In (ii) both halves of the comparison are needed.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- Any THREE of: **longer droughts or dry spells**; **heavy rain in a short time causing floods**; **rivers, streams and wells drying up**; **certain plants or animals disappearing from the area**; **crops failing or maturing at unusual times**; **stronger winds and more storms**; **hotter nights** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: The sign must be a lasting change, not a single day's weather.*\n\n**(c)** [4 marks]\n\n- (i) Any TWO of: **volcanic eruptions**; **changes in the sun's energy**; **changes in ocean currents**; **changes in the earth's orbit or tilt**; **methane from natural wetlands**; **wildfires started by lightning** (1 mark each).\n- (ii) A correct explanation, for example **volcanic ash blocks sunlight so less heat reaches the earth** (1 mark) **and the earth cools for a period** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: A human activity named in (i) earns no mark.*\n\n### Question 2 (12 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- (i) **Radiation (heat and light) from the sun reaching the earth** (1 mark).\n- (ii) **Heat from the earth escaping through the layer into space** (1 mark).\n- (iii) **Heat from the earth sent back to the surface by the layer** (1 mark).\n- (iv) **The layer of greenhouse gases in the atmosphere** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: In (iii) the idea of the heat returning to the earth is essential.*\n\n**(b)** [2 marks]\n\n- Any TWO of: **carbon dioxide**, **methane**, **water vapour**, **nitrous oxide** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: Oxygen and nitrogen are not greenhouse gases and earn no mark.*\n\n**(c)** [3 marks]\n\n- (i) **All the heat radiated by the surface would escape into space** (1 mark); **none would be returned, so the earth would lose heat and be very much colder** (1 mark).\n- (ii) **The temperature rises (the earth becomes warmer)** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Accept 'global warming' in (ii).*\n\n**(d)** [3 marks]\n\n- Any THREE activities each with the correct gas: **burning petrol or diesel - carbon dioxide** (1 mark); **deforestation, charcoal burning or bush burning - carbon dioxide** (1 mark); **cattle rearing, rotting waste in dumps or flooded rice fields - methane** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: No mark for an activity without the gas it adds.*\n\n### Question 3 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- (i) **26.0 °C** (1 mark) and **28.0 °C** (1 mark).\n- (ii) **28.0 - 26.0 = 2.0 °C** (1 mark).\n- (iii) **2.0 ÷ 4 = 0.5 °C per ten years** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: The unit °C is required for the final two marks.*\n\n**(b)** [2 marks]\n\n- Trend: **the mean temperature rises steadily from 1985 to 2025** (1 mark).\n- Meaning: **the district is becoming warmer - its climate is changing** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'The line goes up' alone earns the first mark only.*\n\n**(c)** [4 marks]\n\n- Any FOUR of: **plant and protect trees**; **stop bush burning**; **use improved stoves, gas or solar energy instead of much firewood and charcoal**; **share transport, walk, cycle or use buses**; **switch off lights and use LED lamps**; **compost waste or use a biogas "
