        "text": "At Osu Presbyterian Basic School, Adwoa's class collected the following materials from the school store and from home: copper wire, iron filings, powdered sulphur, table salt, water and air. The teacher asked the class to sort the materials and to study one of them more closely.\n\n**(a)** Explain the terms **element** and **compound** as used in chemistry.\n\n**(b)** Copy and complete the table below in your answer booklet by writing the correct chemical symbol of each element.\n\n| Element | Chemical symbol |\n| --- | --- |\n| Iron | |\n| Sodium | |\n| Copper | |\n\n**(c)** The class put iron filings and powdered sulphur in a dish and stirred them. In another dish, the teacher heated the same two materials together until they glowed and a black solid, iron(II) sulphide, was formed.\n\nState **three** differences between the material in the first dish and the black solid in the second dish.\n\n**(d)** Describe a simple test the class could carry out to show that the material in the **first** dish is a mixture, and state the result they would expect.\n\n---"
