        "number": 1,
        "marks": 10,
        "text": "During a science lesson at Nkawkaw, a teacher switched on a torch, pointed to a solar panel on the roof and asked the class to talk about the energy changes that were taking place around them.\n\n**(a)** (i) What is meant by **conversion of energy**?  **[1 mark]**\n\n(ii) State the **law of conservation of energy**.  **[1 mark]**\n\n(iii) Give the SI unit of energy.  **[1 mark]**\n\n**(b)** State the energy conversion that takes place in each of the following:\n\n(i) a solar panel in sunshine;  **[1 mark]**\n\n(ii) a green leaf making food;  **[1 mark]**\n\n(iii) a coconut falling from a tree.  **[1 mark]**\n\n**(c)** Write the complete **energy chain** that takes place in a dry-cell torch from the moment it is switched on.\n\n**(d)** Using **one** everyday example of each, explain the difference between **conversion** of energy and **conservation** of energy.\n\n---"
