        "number": 1,
        "marks": 10,
        "text": "Madam Afia farms at Akatsi. On the same morning she sowed okro, maize and cassava on three parts of her land. By the end of the year the three crops were at very different stages.\n\n**(a)** (i) What is meant by the **maturity** of a crop?  **[1 mark]**\n\n(ii) State **one** sign that a maize crop is fully mature.  **[1 mark]**\n\n**(b)** (i) Arrange the following stages of the growth of a maize crop in the correct order: **flowering, germination, maturity, seedling, vegetative growth**.  **[2 marks]**\n\n(ii) State what the plant does during the vegetative stage.  **[1 mark]**\n\n**(c)** Crops are often grouped as **early maturing**, **medium maturing** and **late maturing**. Give **one** example of a crop in each group from among the crops grown in your district.\n\n**(d)** Madam Afia wants to have green maize ready to sell at a festival in the third week of December. Maize takes about 10 weeks to reach the green stage. Explain what she should do.\n\n---"
