    "markingScheme": "*General rules: (1) Accept any other correct and relevant answer. (2) In calculations, award the method mark for a correct formula or substitution even when the arithmetic that follows is wrong, and award the final mark only when the unit is given. (3) In circuit diagrams accept the standard symbols or clearly labelled drawings of the components; the circuit must be complete. (4) Accept 'bulb' for 'lamp' and 'battery' for 'cells'. (5) Where a candidate gives more answers than are asked for, mark only the first ones up to the number required. (6) Do not deduct marks for spelling unless the meaning is changed.)*\n\n### Question 1 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [3 marks]\n\n- (i) **Electrical energy to light energy** (accept 'and heat') (1 mark).\n- (ii) **Electrical energy to kinetic (mechanical) energy** (1 mark).\n- (iii) **Electrical energy to heat energy** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: The starting form, electrical energy, must be stated in at least one of the three answers for full credit.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- A **complete (closed) circuit** drawn as a single loop (1 mark).\n- **Correct symbols for the cell and the switch** (1 mark).\n- **Two lamps drawn one after the other in the same path (in series), all parts labelled** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Accept clearly labelled drawings of the components in place of the standard symbols; a circuit with a gap in it loses the first mark.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- **Arrangement or voltage:** in series the lamps are in one path and share the voltage; in parallel each lamp is across the supply and receives the full voltage (1 mark).\n- **Effect of a break:** in series one broken lamp puts off all the lamps; in parallel the other lamps continue to work (accept the current comparison) (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Each mark needs both sides of the comparison.*\n\n**(d)** [2 marks]\n\n- Each lamp **receives the full supply voltage and so lights normally, and each has its own switch** (1 mark).\n- **A lamp that blows does not put out the other lamps**, since the other branches are still complete (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: A bare statement 'parallel is better' earns no mark.*\n\n### Question 2 (12 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- W - **the battery (two cells)** (1 mark).\n- Z - **the switch (open)** (1 mark).\n- C - **the ammeter** (1 mark).\n- D - **a lamp (bulb)** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Accept 'cells' for W; do not accept 'voltmeter' for C.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- (i) **In parallel** (1 mark).\n- (ii) **Lamp X continues to burn (stays on)** (1 mark).\n- (ii) Because **its own branch is still a complete path from the battery**; only the branch carrying Y is broken (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'It goes off' earns no mark, even with a good explanation.*\n\n**(c)** [3 marks]\n\n- (i) **Both X and Y go off** (1 mark).\n- (i) Because **D is in series with the whole parallel section, so the only path from the battery is broken** (1 mark).\n- (ii) **Electrical energy to light energy (and heat energy)** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: In (i) the reason must mention that D is in the main line (in series).*\n\n**(d)** [2 marks]\n\n- Correct formula and substitution: **V = IR = 1.5 × 6** (1 mark).\n- **V = 9 V** (unit required) (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Award the first mark for the correct substitution even if the arithmetic fails.*\n\n### Question 3 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [3 marks]\n\n- (i) **V = IR** (1 mark).\n- (ii) Current: **ampere (A)** (1 mark).\n- (ii) Resistance: **ohm (Ω)** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Accept 'amp' for ampere.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- (i) **I = V/R = 6/3 = 2 A** (1 mark).\n- (ii) Total resistance = **3 + 3 = 6 Ω** (1 mark).\n- (ii) **I = 6/6 = 1 A** (unit required) (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: A candidate who writes 1 A without showing the total resistance earns 1 mark only.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- **R = V/I = 12/0.5** (1 mark).\n- **R = 24 Ω** (unit required) (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: A candidate who writes 6 Ω (having multiplied) earns no marks.*\n\n**(d)** [2 marks]\n\n- **No / the pupil is wrong** (1 mark).\n- **Reason:** "
