        "number": 1,
        "marks": 10,
        "text": "A Basic 9 class at Aflao was asked to look for the action of pressure in the things they use every day: a kitchen knife, a drinking straw, the wide tyres of a tractor and the hose at the washing bay near the school.\n\n**(a)** (i) What is **pressure**?  **[1 mark]**\n\n(ii) Write the formula that connects pressure, force and area.  **[1 mark]**\n\n(iii) Give the SI unit of pressure.  **[1 mark]**\n\n**(b)** Explain, in terms of pressure, why\n\n(i) a knife is sharpened before it is used;  **[1 mark]**\n\n(ii) a tractor used on soft farmland is fitted with wide tyres;  **[1 mark]**\n\n(iii) the foundation of a building is made wider than the wall.  **[1 mark]**\n\n**(c)** Explain how a person is able to draw a drink up a straw.\n\n**(d)** Describe **one** simple activity, other than drinking through a straw, that the class could perform to show the action of pressure. State what would be observed.\n\n---"
