        "text": "During a health week at a junior high school in Takoradi, the school nurse spoke to the pupils about health and disease. She wrote these conditions on the board: cholera, diabetes, measles, high blood pressure, tuberculosis and kwashiorkor.\n\n**(a)** (i) State the definition of **health** given by the World Health Organisation (WHO).  **[2 marks]**\n\n(ii) What is a **disease**?  **[1 mark]**\n\n**(b)** Explain the relationship between health and disease.\n\n**(c)** From the nurse's list, write THREE diseases that are **communicable** and state, for any ONE of them, how it is passed from person to person.  **[3 marks]**\n\n**(d)** A boy in the school has no illness, but he is always alone, unhappy and afraid of his classmates. Using the WHO definition, state whether he is healthy and give a reason.\n\n---"
