        "number": 3,
        "marks": 10,
        "text": "In Basic 7 the pupils studied the housefly and in Basic 8 the mosquito. Their teacher now asked them to compare those life cycles with the one they had just drawn.\n\n**(a)** Copy and complete the table below in your answer booklet.\n\n| | Incomplete metamorphosis | Complete metamorphosis |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Number of stages | | |\n| Name of the young stage | | |\n| Is there a resting (pupal) stage? | | |\n| One example of an insect | | |\n\n**(b)** State **three** differences between a **nymph** and a **larva**.\n\n**(c)** Two pupils kept insects in jars and recorded what they saw.\n\n**Jar 1:** the young that hatched was white and worm-like, fed on rotting food, later became still inside a brown case, and finally came out with wings.\n\n**Jar 2:** the young that hatched looked like a small adult, fed on the same leaves as the adult, and grew bigger after each moult.\n\n(i) State the kind of metamorphosis in each jar.  **[2 marks]**\n\n(ii) Give **one** piece of evidence from Jar 1 for your answer.  **[1 mark]**\n\n---"
