        "number": 1,
        "marks": 10,
        "text": "The Agriculture Club of a Basic 9 school at Asesewa keeps a small garden. The members were asked to collect the waste from the school kitchen, the compound and the poultry house instead of burning it.\n\n**(a)** (i) What is **manure**?  **[1 mark]**\n\n(ii) State **one** way in which manure differs from an inorganic fertiliser.  **[1 mark]**\n\n**(b)** Name **three** types of manure used by farmers.\n\n**(c)** (i) Name **two** plant wastes and **two** animal wastes that the club could use in making manure.  **[2 marks]**\n\n(ii) Name the nutrient for which poultry droppings are especially valued.  **[1 mark]**\n\n**(d)** The club's garden is on a light, sandy soil. Justify the use of manure on such a soil.\n\n---"
