        "text": "Nitrogen makes up by far the largest part of the air around us, yet a maize plant standing in that air can still suffer from a shortage of nitrogen. A Basic 9 class at Ho discussed this puzzle with their teacher.\n\n**(a)** (i) State the approximate percentage of nitrogen in the air.  **[1 mark]**\n\n(ii) Give **one** reason why a green plant cannot use this nitrogen directly.  **[1 mark]**\n\n**(b)** (i) In what form does a green plant take nitrogen from the soil?  **[1 mark]**\n\n(ii) State **two** uses of nitrogen in living things.  **[2 marks]**\n\n**(c)** Explain why the nitrogen cycle is described as a **repeated pattern of change in nature**.\n\n**(d)** The maize on one plot had pale yellow leaves and the plants were short, while the maize on the next plot was tall and dark green.\n\n(i) Name the plant nutrient most likely to be short on the first plot.  **[1 mark]**\n\n(ii) State **one** thing the farmer could do to correct it.  **[1 mark]**\n\n---"
