        "number": 1,
        "marks": 10,
        "text": "A science club at Koforidua held an evening sky-watch. The teacher explained that besides the eight planets, the Sun holds many other bodies in its family.\n\n**(a)** (i) What is the **solar system**?  **[1 mark]**\n\n(ii) Name the force that keeps all the bodies of the solar system moving round the Sun.  **[1 mark]**\n\n**(b)** Name **three** kinds of non-planetary body found in the solar system.\n\n**(c)** (i) State **one** difference between a planet and a natural satellite.  **[1 mark]**\n\n(ii) Give **one** example of each.  **[2 marks]**\n\n**(d)** The Moon is larger than some of the bodies in the solar system, yet it is not called a planet. Explain why.\n\n---"
