        "number": 1,
        "marks": 10,
        "text": "The Basic 9 class of a school at Suhum listed the places of work in and around their town: a sawmill, a cocoa buying shed, a bakery, a group of kente weavers, a taxi station, a palm oil mill and a blacksmith's shop.\n\n**(a)** (i) What is an **industry**?  **[1 mark]**\n\n(ii) Name the THREE main groups into which industries are classified.  **[2 marks]**\n\n**(b)** From the class list, name\n\n(i) ONE primary industry;  **[1 mark]**\n\n(ii) TWO secondary industries;  **[2 marks]**\n\n(iii) ONE service industry.  **[1 mark]**\n\n**(c)** Write down, in the correct order, the FOUR stages through which the palm fruits of the town become palm oil sold in the market, and name the stage at which a scientific separation takes place.  **[3 marks]**\n\n---"
