    "markingScheme": "*General rules: (1) Accept any other correct and relevant answer. (2) Accept the local name of a plant or a material provided the plant meant is clear. (3) Where a use is asked for, the plant part AND the use must both be clear; 'the tree is used' earns no mark. (4) Where a candidate gives more answers than are asked for, mark only the first ones up to the number required. (5) Diagrams need not be works of art; marks are for correct shape and correct labels. (6) Do not deduct marks for spelling unless the meaning is changed.)*\n\n### Question 1 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [5 marks]\n\n- A - **root** (1 mark).\n- B - **stem** (1 mark).\n- C - **leaf** (1 mark).\n- D - **flower** (1 mark).\n- E - **fruit** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: One mark for each part; no half marks.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- (i) **Absorbs water and mineral salts / anchors the plant** (1 mark).\n- (ii) **Supports the plant and conducts water and food** (1 mark).\n- (iii) **Makes food by photosynthesis** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: One correct function in each case is enough.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- Method: **planting stem cuttings** (1 mark).\n- Advantage: **the new plants are exactly like the parent and mature earlier** (accept: no seed need be bought) (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'Cutting' alone is accepted for the method.*\n\n### Question 2 (12 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- Cassava - **stem cuttings** (1 mark).\n- Yam - **setts cut from the tuber** (1 mark).\n- Plantain - **suckers** (1 mark).\n- Maize - **seeds (grains)** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: The table must be copied; four correct entries earn the marks.*\n\n**(b)** [4 marks]\n\n- (i) **Maize stover and groundnut haulms** (1 mark); **dried and fed to cattle, sheep and goats, especially in the dry season** (1 mark).\n- (ii) **Mucuna (a leguminous plant)** (accept leaves and crop residues for compost) (1 mark); **grown and dug into the soil as green manure, adding nitrogen and organic matter** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: The material must come from the list given.*\n\n**(c)** [4 marks]\n\n- Any FOUR, each naming a material and its use: **odum timber - building, furniture or carving**; **bamboo or palm fronds - roofing, fencing, baskets, mats or brooms**; **bark or leaves - herbal medicine**; **palm fronds - ceremonies and festivals**; **wood - charcoal for cooking**; **leaves or bark - dye for cloth** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: No mark for a use given without the material, or the reverse.*\n\n### Question 3 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- W - **planting (propagation) of a new cassava crop** (1 mark).\n- X - **mulching the soil round the plant** (1 mark).\n- Y - **housing birds or small animals, or carrying produce** (1 mark).\n- Z - **a natural pesticide for controlling insect pests** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: The purpose, not merely a description of the picture, is required.*\n\n**(b)** [4 marks]\n\n- (i) Any TWO of: **reduces loss of water from the soil**; **checks the growth of weeds**; **keeps the soil cool**; **protects the soil from heavy rain and erosion**; **adds humus as it rots** (1 mark each).\n- (ii) Any TWO of: **cheap and made from local material**; **leaves little harmful residue on the crop**; **safer for the farmer, the consumer and useful insects**; **always available without buying** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: Two distinct points are needed in each part.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- **Crush or pound the neem leaves and soak them in water overnight** (1 mark).\n- **Strain the liquid through a cloth before pouring it into the sprayer** (accept adding a little soap to make it stick) (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: The straining step is essential for the second mark.*\n\n### Question 4 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- Roofing - **grass stems and palm fronds (leaves)** (1 mark).\n- Stool - **the trunk (woody stem) of a tree** (1 mark).\n- Basket - **stems, leaf strips or fibres of raffia, cane or palm** (1 mark).\n- Herbal medicine - **bark, leaves or roots** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: The table must be copied; four correc"
